From eab8cd731af148bb31aacdf9af4049d36089be39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:48:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] feat(golem): open, seed and close the store of the
 plugins in golem run

The store keeps the data of the ports in one SQLite file, but golem run
never opens it, so no port can keep a home, a mail or a permission, and
a server whose store could not open would boot without its data.

golem run now follows the steps of okf/store.md. It opens
golem-store.db beside world/ after it read the launch and before it
installs the plugins, so a store that does not open stops the start
before the JVM exists. A store without a group of the permissions gets
the seed of config/permissions.toml of the server, or the seed of the
Golem repository that the binary holds when the server has none, which
it loads into golem-permissions first and names on the log. The runtime
gets a clone of the store. Once the JVM ended, golem run closes the
store and exits with 1 when a change did not reach the file. A JVM that
ends through System.exit never returns, so the callback of the exit
hook closes the store there, and a signal before the JVM exists closes
it before golem exits.

The binary now holds the seed, so build.rs counts the file
config/permissions.toml among the files whose change makes a build
dirty.

